# Changelog

All notable changes to this project are documented in this file.

The format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project intends to adopt [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/)
once it reaches a stable `1.0` release. Until then, breaking changes may land
without a major version bump.

## [Unreleased]

- Added `LICENSE`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `SECURITY.md`, and this changelog.
- Added GHCR delivery for the LangGraph and ADK images, including non-publishing
  pull-request image scans, Trivy SARIF results, BuildKit OCI SBOM/provenance
  attestations, and published-digest smoke tests.
- Added Linux AMD64/ARM64 image publication and a dedicated WSL2 self-hosted
  GitHub Actions runner for CI and release jobs.
- Hardened runtime images by removing build-only Python tooling, upgraded the
  LangChain/LangGraph stack past known fixable vulnerabilities, and retained a
  blocking Trivy gate for fixable HIGH/CRITICAL findings.
- Added container consumption and release-operation documentation.
- Added richer workflow expressions, deterministic nested-loop scoping, and
  broader Open Workflow and Agent Spec conformance fixtures.
- Added application-bundle compatibility validation for mixed workflow DSL
  versions, unsupported Agent Spec versions, unresolved agent calls, and
  explicitly referenced MCP tool bindings.
- Added graceful runner shutdown, in-flight request draining, MCP lifecycle
  cleanup, cancellation-state coverage, and checkpoint restart-reuse tests.
- Added checked-in OpenAPI documents for both engines, generator drift checks,
  API and expression guides, and a static architecture diagram.
- Expanded Git and Docker ignore policies for secrets, caches, local runtime
  state, scan output, and build artifacts; added repository line-ending rules.
- Upgraded GitHub Actions to Node 24-compatible releases and retained the
  dedicated self-hosted WSL2 runner quality, scan, smoke-test, and ARM64 gates.
- Documented that both engine compilers currently wrap the shared
  `InMemoryEngine` interpreter instead of mapping workflow task trees onto
  native LangGraph/ADK constructs, and planned the replacement as
  `COMPILE-001`..`COMPILE-015` in `TODO.md` (no behavior change yet).
- Documented that the declared Agent Spec `memory` field is parsed but not
  wired into execution by either engine, and planned a pluggable
  `MemoryStore` abstraction (in-memory/SQLite/Postgres/third-party backends
  with availability health checks) as `MEM-001`..`MEM-006` in `TODO.md` (no
  behavior change yet).
- Documented that each engine's default model (`gpt-4o-mini` /
  `gemini-2.0-flash`) is hardcoded inline with no environment override, and
  planned a shared `resolve_model()` helper with `DEFAULT_MODEL`/
  `OPENAI_DEFAULT_MODEL`/`GOOGLE_DEFAULT_MODEL` env vars covering every
  agent and sub-agent either engine compiles, as `MODEL-001`..`MODEL-005`
  in `TODO.md` (no behavior change yet).

## [0.1.0]

Initial workspace: Open Workflow and Open Agent Specification loaders and
validation, framework-neutral IR, deterministic in-memory execution,
LangGraph and Google ADK compilers/runners with OpenAI-compatible APIs,
optional SQLite checkpoints, MCP adapters, Docker images, and CI. See
`TODO.md` for the detailed, itemized history of this release.
